From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 23:30:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] AMLLatency: log the lead sample by sample after a start

The lead - how far the audio leads the picture at the box output - is the
one figure a start or resume is judged by: a clock step moves its two
halves in opposite directions and cancels in it. The report gives it once
a minute as an average, which hides where a start landed and how the trim
walked it out.

For 30 s after the matcher re-arms (a start, a seek, a resume), log every
2 s the lead, its audio and picture halves, and the filtered value the
trim acts on. Nothing else changes.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/AMLLatency.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/AMLLatency.cpp
@@ -52,6 +52,11 @@ constexpr double TIME_BETWEEN_REPORTS =
 //! rather than the last sample.
 constexpr double LEAD_TAU = 5.0 * DVD_TIME_BASE;
 
+// How long after a start or resume the lead is logged sample by sample, and how
+// often: the minute report averages away exactly the part a start is judged by.
+constexpr double LEAD_LOG_WINDOW = 30.0 * DVD_TIME_BASE;
+constexpr double LEAD_LOG_EVERY = 2.0 * DVD_TIME_BASE;
+
 //! A step this big is not the loop moving the figure - at the most it may ever
 //! ask for, it moves it a hundred times slower than this per sample. Set below a
 //! refresh period so a swallowed one is caught, and well above the ripple.
@@ -657,6 +662,8 @@ void CAMLLatency::Update(
 
       if (!m_haveLead)
       {
+        m_leadLogUntil = absolute + LEAD_LOG_WINDOW;
+        m_leadLogAt = absolute - LEAD_LOG_EVERY;
         m_leadFilt = lead;
         m_haveLead = true;
         m_leadOdd = 0.0;
@@ -698,6 +705,24 @@ void CAMLLatency::Update(
         }
       }
       m_leadAt = absolute;
+
+      if (absolute < m_leadLogUntil && absolute - m_leadLogAt >= LEAD_LOG_EVERY)
+      {
+        m_leadLogAt = absolute;
+        // Unsettled, the frame on screen and the one waited for are printed too:
+        // the two tell a picture that is off from a timestamp base that is.
+        if (m_settled)
+          CLog::Log(LOGDEBUG, LOGVIDEO,
+                    "CAMLLatency: lead {:+.2f}ms (audio {:+.2f}, picture {:+.2f}), filtered {:+.2f}ms",
+                    lead / 1000.0, audioSyncError / 1000.0, alignment / 1000.0,
+                    m_leadFilt / 1000.0);
+        else
+          CLog::Log(LOGDEBUG, LOGVIDEO,
+                    "CAMLLatency: lead {:+.2f}ms (audio {:+.2f}, picture {:+.2f}) unsettled: "
+                    "clock {:.3f}s, on screen {:.3f}s, waiting for {:.3f}s",
+                    lead / 1000.0, audioSyncError / 1000.0, alignment / 1000.0,
+                    clockNow / DVD_TIME_BASE, shownUs / DVD_TIME_BASE, m_key / 90000.0);
+      }
     }
 
     if (absolute - m_since >= TIME_BETWEEN_REPORTS)
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/AMLLatency.h
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/AMLLatency.h
@@ -198,6 +198,8 @@ private:
   double m_leadOdd{0.0};     //!< how long the figure has disagreed with the filter
   double m_leadAt{0.0};      //!< when that was last advanced
   bool m_haveLead{false};
+  double m_leadLogUntil{0.0}; //!< end of the per-sample log after a start
+  double m_leadLogAt{0.0};
   double m_driftAlign{0.0};  //!< the same at the previous report
   double m_driftWalkUs{0.0};
   int m_driftFrames{0};  //!< refreshes swallowed, the walk's own check
